    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/technical-real-estate-project-manager--client-side-project-management--18-month-fixed-term-contract-f35a09": {
      "title": "Technical Real Estate Project Manager",
      "description": "Technical Real Estate Project Manager – Client-Side Project Management – 18-month Fixed-Term Contract F/H - Temporary contract 18 months in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Technical Real Estate Project Manager – Client-Side Project Management – 18-month Fixed-Term Contract F/H Apply to this job Technical Real Estate Project Manager – Client-Side Project Management – 18-month Fixed-Term Contract F/H I apply Published on               \n                25/09/2026 Contract type: Temporary contract\n- 18 months Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description As part of its real estate projects across Europe, ESCP is looking for a professional with extensive technical expertise in building construction to support and safeguard its real estate projects from design through to completion, acting on behalf of the client or end users. Within the Real Estate Department, you will provide technical expertise throughout the projects and contribute to informed decision-making by the Department. Your role will help ensure that technical solutions are aligned with project requirements, budgets, timelines and quality standards. Key responsibilities You will be responsible for: Reviewing design studies and assessing the proposed technical solutions. Identifying and anticipating technical, financial, contractual and scheduling considerations requiring particular attention. Assessing the impact of technical choices on costs, timelines and quality. Reviewing proposals submitted by architects and engineering teams, design consultancies, contractors and project management teams. Reviewing budgets, cost estimates, schedules and key milestones. Participating in project reviews and providing well-supported recommendations to inform decision-making. Collaborating with campus teams and the various project partners across Europe. Profile required Skills and experience Engineering degree, building engineering qualification or equivalent education. At least 10 to 15 years of experience in the design, construction and/or management of real estate projects. Experience in client-side project management or client-side project management consultancy. Extensive technical expertise in building construction is essential. Ability to assess complex issues, identify areas requiring particular attention and propose appropriate solutions. Experience within an engineering consultancy or general contractor would be an advantage. Experience working on projects across several European countries is highly desirable. Experience with commercial buildings, higher education facilities, hospitality projects or public-access buildings would be an advantage. Professional proficiency in English is essential. Ability to work effectively with multicultural teams. Réf: f35a093c-21b2-423d-8a56-0c3ed77ff6a4 Apply Technical Real Estate Project Manager – Client-Side Project Management – 18-month Fixed-Term Contract F/H Temporary contract - 18 months Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Pourquoi souhaitez vous rejoindre ESCP Business School ? As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Technical Real Estate Project Manager – Client-Side Project Management – 18-month Fixed-Term Contract F/H Temporary contract\n- 18 months Full time Paris I apply Internships officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Stage Growth & Conversion (SEO & UX) F/H Apprenticeship\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
