    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/hr-coordinator-maternity-cover-f8c559": {
      "title": "HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M",
      "description": "HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M - Temporary contract 16 months in London | Découvrez nos offres Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP Plus See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN EN FR See our jobs HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M Apply to this job HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M I apply Published on               \n                28/09/2026 Subsidiary : ESCP Business School London Campus Contract type: Temporary contract\n- 16 months Work time: Part time Location London Salary 22368 GBP (£) - 22368 GBP (£) / year The company Founded in 1819, ESCP Business School develops responsible, globally minded leaders through a European, multicultural approach. Across six campuses in Berlin, London, Madrid, Paris, Turin and Warsaw, ESCP welcomes 9,000+ students and 5,000 managers from 130 nationalities. Its portfolio spans undergraduate, postgraduate, MBA, PhD and executive education, with programmes consistently ranked among the world’s best. Post description FTC until March 2028 Part time, 28 hours per week (0.8 FTE) £22,368 actual salary (FTE salary £27,960) Hybrid working available ESCP Business School London is seeking a proactive and enthusiastic HR Coordinator to join our small HR team on a temporary basis covering a period of maternity leave,  to help us continue to deliver an exceptional HR service across the School. As a first point of contact for HR queries, you’ll provide responsive and professional support to colleagues across the School, while working closely with the wider HR team to deliver our departmental priorities. This is a varied, hands-on generalist role offering exposure to the full employee lifecycle and the wider HR remit, including payroll administration, recruitment, onboarding and learning and development. You’ll play a key role in ensuring our day-to-day HR operations run smoothly and effectively. This is a fantastic opportunity for someone looking to pursue a career in HR, take ownership of a varied workload and develop their skills within a dynamic, international higher education environment. Profile required Knowledge, Skills and Experience The ideal candidate for this role will have a pro-active and solutions focused approach. Being able to quickly adapt to new systems and processes, and a willingness to learn will be essential for success in this role. Essential Requirements: Previous experience in an administrative role, ideally within an HR department. Strong organisational skills and good time management. Works to a high level of accuracy, with a keen eye for detail. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. A basic understanding of HR principles and processes. Proficiency in Microsoft Office / Google Suite (especially Word and Excel) is essential. Experience of using online systems, databases and/or electronic filing systems, with experience of using an HRIS particularly desirable. Able to work independently, and seek additional support when necessary. Ability to handle sensitive information with discretion. Desirable Requirements: Previous experience within an HR role. Previous working experience in the Higher Education sector. CIPD Level 3 or working towards it (or equivalent experience). Experience of contributing to departmental goals. Main Duties and Responsibilities: Support the HR team in delivering a full range of staff administration services, including recruitment, onboarding, payroll administration, contract management, and leaver processes. Coordinate HR documentation and maintain accurate employee records in line with data protection and compliance standards. Administer staff benefits and assist with general HR correspondence and day-to-day operations. Support recruitment campaigns, pre-employment checks, and onboarding to ensure a smooth employee experience. Assist with HR projects and provide general administrative support as needed. Réf: f8c559f5-39b2-40de-9147-2233f173512b Apply HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School LONDON Temporary contract - 16 months Part time London 22368 GBP (£) - 22368 GBP (£) / year Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Do you currently have, or will you have, the right to work in the UK through March 2028 without requiring employer sponsorship? Please note that this role is not eligible for visa sponsorship. * Yes No Do you have experience working in an administrative role? If yes, please provide brief details of your relevant experience. * How would you describe your proficiency in using Microsoft Office or Google Workspace applications? * Please tell us what attracted you to this role. * As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 16 months Part time London I apply Procurement Officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Technical Real Estate Project Manager – Client-Side Project Management – 18-month Fixed-Term Contract F/H Temporary contract\n- 18 months Full time Paris I apply Internships officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
