    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/apprenticeship--procurement-it--property-7a0aac": {
      "title": "Apprenticeship",
      "description": "Apprenticeship – Procurement IT / Property F/H - Apprenticeship 12 months in Paris | Découvrez nos offres Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP Plus See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN EN FR See our jobs Apprenticeship – Procurement IT / Property F/H Apply to this job Apprenticeship – Procurement IT / Property F/H I apply Published on               \n                05/10/2026 Contract type: Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description Support the day-to-day activities of the Procurement Department by managing the administrative and operational aspects of purchasing, suppliers, contracts, tenders, invoicing, and reporting, in order to ensure business continuity and optimize expenditure. Key Responsibilities Create and monitor purchase requisitions and purchase orders in SAP through to receipt. Monitor purchase orders, deliveries, and supplies to ensure timely fulfilment. Manage administrative relationships with suppliers and maintain supplier master data and records. Receive, review, and reconcile invoices against purchase orders, and prepare them for approval in coordination with the relevant departments. Monitor payments in collaboration with the Accounting team and contribute to periodic financial closing activities. Identify, track, and resolve discrepancies and disputes related to purchase orders, contracts, or invoices through to resolution. Maintain dashboards, produce performance indicators and KPIs, and contribute to internal audits. Act as a business partner to the IT and Real Estate teams, supporting and optimizing the entire process from requirements definition through to payment. Profile required Required Skills Good understanding of Procure-to-Pay (P2P) processes. Proficiency in ERP systems, ideally SAP, and advanced Excel skills, including advanced functions and PivotTables. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, ability to prioritize, and analytical thinking. Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to collaborate effectively with business teams, Finance, Accounting, and suppliers. Candidate Profile Previous internship experience in a similar role. Professional working proficiency in English. Preferred work-study schedule: 3 days in the company / 2 days at school, or 3 weeks in the company / 1 week at school. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: 7a0aacfe-fcca-4fab-8f42-4451c092fff1 Apply Apprenticeship – Procurement IT / Property F/H Apprenticeship - 12 months Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est le rythme de votre alternance ecolé/entreprise ? * A partir de quelle date pouvez vous commencer votre contrat d'alternance ? * Quelle est la durée d'alternance recherchée ? * Quel est votre niveau d'anglais * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Apprenticeship – Procurement IT / Property F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 16 months Part time London I apply Procurement Officer F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply Technical Real Estate Project Manager – Client-Side Project Management – 18-month Fixed-Term Contract F/H Temporary contract\n- 18 months Full time Paris I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
