    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/senior-marketing-manager-6ec0e5": {
      "title": "Senior Marketing Manager F/M",
      "description": "Senior Marketing Manager F/M - Permanent contract in London | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Senior Marketing Manager F/M Apply to this job Senior Marketing Manager F/M I apply Update on \n                07/10/2026 Subsidiary : ESCP Business School London Campus Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location London Salary 46788 GBP (£) - 48679 GBP (£) / year The company ESCP Business School was founded in 1819. The School has chosen to teach responsible leadership, open to the world and based on European multiculturalism. Six campuses in Berlin, London, Madrid, Paris, Turin and Warsaw are the stepping stones that allow students to experience this European approach to management. In 2025, ESCP was ranked 4th in the FT European Business Schools rankings. Several generations of entrepreneurs and managers were trained in the firm belief that the business world may feed society in a positive way. Each year, ESCP welcomes 9000+ students and 5000 managers from 130 different nationalities. We offer a full range of full-time degree programmes from our generalist BSc in Management, Master in Management (FT-ranked 6th worldwide), and MBA in International Management (FT-ranked 22nd worldwide) to a portfolio of over 20 specialist Master-level programmes, including our MSc in Finance (FT-ranked 1st worldwide), and to PhD. We also deliver executive education programmes including the Executive MBA (FT-ranked 5th worldwide), specialist Master-level executive degree programmes, and Executive PhD. All of the programmes include a multi-campus experience. ESCP contributes to the learning and development of executives and managers at some of the world’s leading companies through the development and provision of customised courses. Role Details Type of Employment: Permanent Hours: 35 hours per week (1.0 FTE) Salary: £46,788.89 to £48,679 per annum, dependent on experience Location: 527 Finchley Rd, London NW3 7BG Reporting to: Director of Marketing, Recruitment and Admissions Role Summary The Senior Marketing Manager is a key role within the London Campus Marketing, Recruitment and Admissions (MAR) team, leading student recruitment marketing across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes while retaining direct ownership of an allocated programme portfolio. The postholder will lead and develop the London Campus marketing function, setting priorities and ways of working and ensuring budgets, resources and agency support are aligned with recruitment objectives and deployed effectively. Using market and audience insight, digital acquisition, content, CRM, brand and analytics, they will identify opportunities, optimise investment and continuously improve marketing performance and the prospective student journey. Working closely with Recruitment and Admissions, programme and faculty teams, European marketing colleagues, Brand and Communications, and external agencies, the postholder will provide strategic marketing expertise, influence stakeholders and ensure alignment with recruitment and wider School priorities. This is a hands-on role, combining management of the London Campus marketing function with direct accountability for programme marketing in ESCP’s international, multi-campus environment. Duties and Responsibilities Include: Marketing Strategy & Planning: Act as the senior marketing lead for student recruitment at the London Campus, working with the Director of Marketing, Recruitment and Admissions to shape the overall direction, priorities and performance of the marketing function. Own and deliver the annual student recruitment marketing strategy across the London Campus undergraduate and postgraduate portfolio, including direct accountability for an allocated portfolio of programmes and the development of programme-level plans aligned with recruitment targets and institutional priorities. Translate recruitment objectives into evidence-based marketing strategies covering target audiences, priority markets, positioning, messaging, channels, candidate journeys, investment and performance measures, working closely with Marketing, Recruitment and Admissions colleagues to develop integrated plans. Lead market, audience and competitor analysis to inform programme positioning, identify growth opportunities and emerging markets, audiences and channels, and make evidence-based recommendations on future marketing activity and investment. Determine marketing priorities and recommend the allocation of resources and investment across programmes, audiences, markets and channels to maximise impact and return, while identifying efficiencies and synergies through shared campaigns, content, audiences, technologies, agencies and resources. Act as the senior marketing partner to programme and Recruitment and Admissions stakeholders, providing strategic advice and constructive challenge on positioning, value propositions, audiences, campaign priorities and investment, while ensuring activity is distinctive, compelling, evidence-based and consistent with the ESCP brand. Support key institutional and external initiatives, including the annual QS Masters in Marketing ranking submission. Demand Generation and Candidate Marketing: Own the London Campus approach to demand generation and candidate marketing, ensuring activity drives both the volume and quality of prospective student demand and contributes measurably to recruitment objectives, with direct accountability for campaigns across an allocated programme portfolio. Lead the development, delivery and optimisation of integrated, multi-channel campaigns across the London Campus programme portfolio, setting the strategic direction for audience segmentation, targeting and paid media across search, social, display and emerging channels, with investment and optimisation driven by performance and priority markets. Lead the development and optimisation of candidate journeys from awareness and enquiry through to application, working closely with Recruitment and Admissions to align lead generation, candidate engagement, application and conversion activity, with clear hand-offs and shared ownership of funnel performance. Support the Recruitment team in developing compelling CRM conversion campaigns that engage prospective students and drive progression through the recruitment funnel. Agency & Supplier Management Manage media agency and supplier relationships, setting strategic briefs, objectives, budgets and KPIs, and ensuring multi-platform activity across Google Ads, LLMs, Facebook, LinkedIn, TikTok and other channels is aligned with programme and recruitment priorities. Provide strategic oversight and constructive challenge of agency recommendations and campaign approaches, holding agencies and suppliers accountable for delivery, performance, quality and value for money, and directing optimisation or changes where required. Ensure external creative, digital, media and print resources are deployed effectively across programme priorities, providing strategic oversight of high-quality assets in collaboration with the Marketing Executive, Brand and Communications colleagues and external suppliers. Content & Digital Marketing Develop and oversee the digital marketing strategy across paid social, SEO/SEM, programme webpages, landing pages, third-party platforms and marketing automation, using performance and audience insight to prioritise optimisation and improve recruitment outcomes. Set the content strategy and priorities across the programme portfolio, ensuring content, propositions and messaging are audience-led, differentiated, aligned with programme positioning and effectively communicate ESCP’s distinctive strengths across markets and audiences. Provide strategic direction and approval for priority campaign content and creative assets, working with Brand and Communications to prioritise video, photography, social media, AI visibility and other content that supports awareness, acquisition and conversion, while ensuring quality and brand consistency. Support the Recruitment team with CRM communications, ensuring effective segmentation, personalisation and nurturing throughout the prospective student journey, while identifying and evaluating emerging digital channels, technologies and approaches to improve marketing effectiveness and candidate engagement. Budget and resource management: Own and manage the student recruitment marketing budget across the London Campus programme portfolio within agreed parameters, working with the Director of Marketing, Recruitment and Admissions on annual budget planning, resource requirements and future investment priorities. Make and recommend investment and resource allocation decisions across programmes, markets, audiences and channels, guided by strategic priorities, recruitment objectives and evidence of performance. Monitor expenditure, forecasts and return on marketing investment, ensuring activity remains within agreed budgets and financial controls, and reallocating resources where evidence indicates opportunities to improve performance. Establish and monitor campaign and media agency KPIs, working with the Marketing Executive to deliver weekly and monthly reporting on spend, ROI and campaign effectiveness, providing actionable insights to senior management and stakeholders. Stakeholder Leadership & Accountability Act as the senior marketing partner to Recruitment and Admissions, programme directors, faculty and London Campus stakeholders, providing expert, evidence-based advice and constructive feedback while ensuring marketing priorities and requirements are clearly understood and effectively managed. Work closely with European marketing and recruitment colleagues, representing London Campus priorities and ensuring alignment with wider ESCP initiatives, strategies and opportunities. Advise the Director of Marketing, Recruitment and Admissions on marketing priorities, investment, resource allocation, programme performance and growth opportunities, clearly communicating performance, risks and recommendations to support accountability and timely decision-making. Line Management & Team Development Lead and develop the London Campus marketing function, fostering a collaborative, accountable and high-performing culture across the programme portfolio, with a focus on creativity, innovation, knowledge-sharing and continuous improvement. Line manages the Marketing Executive, setting clear objectives, priorities, performance expectations and programme responsibilities, while supporting their development and effectiveness. Person Specification Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration or a related field, or equivalent professional experience. Significant senior-level marketing experience, with responsibility for developing and delivering integrated marketing strategies and measurable recruitment or commercial outcomes. Strong expertise in digital acquisition, performance marketing and analytics, with the ability to use data to optimise campaigns, investment and decision-making. Experience managing marketing budgets and allocating resources across competing priorities. Strong understanding of brand management, audience positioning and the development of compelling programme propositions. Experience managing external media, creative and digital agencies and holding partners accountable for performance. Proven experience of leading and developing team members and working effectively with senior stakeholders. Excellent communication and influencing skills, with the ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced, international and multicultural environment. Fluent written and spoken English; additional languages are an advantage. Experience or understanding of higher education, business education or international student recruitment is desirable. Benefits 30 days annual leave Hybrid working available (3 days on site, 2 days from home) Company pension scheme with exceptional employer contributions Optional private Dental & GP cover (after completion of probationary period) Réf: 6ec0e581-767b-4ee6-9e7d-07d463dcb120 Apply Senior Marketing Manager F/M ESCP Business School LONDON Permanent contract Full time London 46788 GBP (£) - 48679 GBP (£) / year Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Qualification Certificates Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. CV / Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Do you currently have, or will you have, the right to work in the UK to undertake this role without requiring employer sponsorship? Please note that this role is not eligible for visa sponsorship. * Yes No What attracted you to this role? * How do your skills and experiences align with the person specification of this role? * What is your current notice period? * As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Senior Marketing Manager F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Permanent contract Full time London I apply Legal Apprentice – GDPR & Contracts F/H Internship\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Apprenticeship – Procurement IT / Property F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 16 months Part time London I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
