    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/legal-apprentice--gdpr--contracts-6514fe": {
      "title": "Legal Apprentice",
      "description": "Legal Apprentice – GDPR & Contracts F/H - Internship 6 months in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Legal Apprentice – GDPR & Contracts F/H Apply to this job Legal Apprentice – GDPR & Contracts F/H I apply Published on               \n                06/10/2026 Contract type: Internship\n- 6 months Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description As part of its activities, ESCP Business School is seeking a legal apprentice to support its legal team on matters relating to the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and contract law. Main responsibilities 1. Personal data protection – GDPR • Help monitor compliance with the GDPR in relation to the processing of personal data. • Help update the data processing register and documentation relating to data protection. • Help draft and review privacy policies, privacy notices and internal procedures. • Assist with the analysis of contracts involving the processing of personal data, in particular data processing agreements. • Monitor legal developments regarding regulatory changes and recommendations from the CNIL. 2. Contract law • Assist with the drafting, analysis and review of contracts. • Help to identify legal risks and analyse contractual clauses. • Help to review and update contract templates. • Keep track of contractual documentation. • Help to analyse contracts drafted in French and English. Profile required A student in the first or second year of a Master’s degree in business law, contract law, digital law or data protection. • Fluency in English is essential, both written and spoken, in order to analyse and process legal documents in English. • Good knowledge of contract law and a keen interest in data protection. • Excellent analytical, summarising and legal drafting skills. • Meticulous, able to work independently, well-organised and able to maintain confidentiality. • Previous experience in a legal department or law firm would be an advantage. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: 6514fe77-b2b0-46ea-a98c-b4e27d4d18ba Apply Legal Apprentice – GDPR & Contracts F/H Internship - 6 months Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est le rythme de votre alternance ecolé/entreprise ? * A partir de quelle date pouvez vous commencer votre contrat d'alternance ? * Quelle est la durée d'alternance recherchée ? * Quel est votre niveau d'anglais * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Senior Marketing Manager F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Permanent contract Full time London I apply Legal Apprentice – GDPR & Contracts F/H Internship\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Apprenticeship – Procurement IT / Property F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply HR Coordinator (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 16 months Part time London I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
